# Overrides the root .clang-tidy for test sources only. See issue #284.
#
# bugprone-unchecked-optional-access is off here because every occurrence in this
# tree (14/14, measured clearing #284's backlog) was the same false positive: a
# Catch2 REQUIRE(opt.has_value()) immediately followed by REQUIRE(opt->field ...).
# The check's dataflow analysis doesn't recognise REQUIRE as a guard (it looks for
# if/branch patterns, not assertion macros), so it can never pass for that idiom --
# and production code (StratEngine/) has zero occurrences of the pattern at all, so
# there's nothing this check protects here that a real bug would slip through.
# Left enabled in the root config for StratEngine/, where it still could catch one.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access
